<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="Spend cube: suppliers resolved, spend classified, contract coverage and concentration by category.">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'><rect width='32' height='32' fill='%23EEF2EF'/><rect x='2' y='2' width='17' height='28' fill='%231F6F50'/><rect x='21' y='2' width='9' height='16' fill='%23C27D1A'/><rect x='21' y='20' width='9' height='10' fill='%23E9E4D4'/></svg>">
<style>
@font-face {
  font-family: "Public Sans";
  src: url(data:font/woff2;base64,{{ font }}) format("woff2");
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-display: swap;
}
:root {
  --ledger: #EEF2EF;
  --sheet: #FFFFFF;
  --ink: #102A23;
  --muted: #55665E;
  --rule: #C6D3CB;
  --covered: #1F6F50;
  --exposed: #C27D1A;
  --risk: #9C2F2F;
  color-scheme: light;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--ledger);
  color: var(--ink);
  font: 16px/1.55 "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.page { max-width: 1168px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 44px 24px 64px; }
h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; line-height: 1.08; font-weight: 800; margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 750; margin: 0 0 6px; }
.period { color: var(--muted); margin: 6px 0 0; }
.verdict { font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.38; max-width: 36em; margin: 32px 0 28px; font-weight: 400; }
.verdict strong { font-weight: 750; }
.verdict .out { color: #8A5510; }
.facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0; margin: 0 0 40px; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
.facts div { padding: 12px 18px 0 0; }
.facts dt { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
.facts dd { margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 750; line-height: 1.15; }
.facts dd small { display: block; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 3px; }
section { margin-bottom: 52px; }
.lede { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 16px; max-width: 70ch; }
figure { margin: 0; }
.treemap svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; }
.legend { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); flex-wrap: wrap; }
.ramp { display: flex; height: 10px; width: 220px; }
.ramp span { flex: 1; }
.two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 48px; align-items: start; }
.pareto svg { width: 100%; height: auto; font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; }
.pareto .grid { stroke: var(--rule); stroke-dasharray: 2 4; }
.pareto .axis { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--muted); }
.pareto .marker { stroke: var(--covered); stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
.pareto .callout { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 650; fill: var(--ink); }
.findings { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.findings li { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 14px 1fr auto; gap: 4px 12px; }
.findings .swatch { width: 14px; height: 14px; margin-top: 5px; }
.findings .cat { font-weight: 650; }
.findings .amt { font-weight: 650; text-align: right; }
.findings .msg { grid-column: 2 / 4; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--sheet); }
th { text-align: left; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 650; color: var(--muted); padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
td { padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
.n { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
td .sub { display: block; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); }
td.up { color: var(--risk); font-weight: 650; }
.cov { display: inline-block; width: 46px; height: 8px; background: #E3E8E4; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 8px; }
.cov span { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--covered); }
.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
.merge { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.merge .to { font-weight: 650; }
.merge .from { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
.stack { display: flex; height: 26px; margin: 12px 0 10px; }
.stack span { display: block; height: 100%; }
.stack-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 22px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
.stack-legend i { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: -1px; }
.method { columns: 2; column-gap: 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
.method p { margin: 0 0 12px; break-inside: avoid; }
footer { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
footer a { color: var(--ink); }
@media (max-width: 860px) {
  .two { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .facts { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); row-gap: 16px; }
  .method { columns: 1; }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .page { padding: 28px 16px 48px; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; }
  .verdict { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .treemap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .treemap svg { min-width: 680px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="page">
  <header>
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p class="period">Purchase order lines posted {{ first }} to {{ last }}. Amounts in euro.{% if scope|length <= 3 %} Scope: {{ scope|join(", ") }}.{% endif %}</p>
  </header>

  <p class="verdict">
    <strong>{{ t.spend|eur_short }}</strong> went to <strong>{{ t.suppliers }} suppliers</strong>.
    <span class="out"><strong>{{ (1 - t.on_contract_share)|pct }}</strong> of it was bought outside a contract</span>,
    including <strong>{{ t.maverick_spend|eur_short }}</strong> in categories where a contract already exists.
  </p>

  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>Supplier names resolved</dt><dd>{{ t.raw_names }} to {{ t.suppliers }}<small>spellings merged into suppliers{% if t.multi_member_groups %}, in {{ t.groups }} groups{% endif %}</small></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Spend classified</dt><dd>{{ t.classified_share|pct }}<small>{{ review_count }} lines left for review</small></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Spend on contract</dt><dd>{{ t.on_contract_share|pct }}<small>by value, across all categories</small></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Long tail</dt><dd>{{ t.tail_suppliers }} suppliers<small>share the last 5% of spend</small></dd></div>
  </dl>

  <section>
    <h2>Where the money goes, and how much of it is under contract</h2>
    <p class="lede">Each tile is a category, sized by spend. Ochre tiles are bought mostly outside contracts; green tiles mostly on them.</p>
    <figure class="treemap">
      {{ treemap|safe }}
      <figcaption class="legend">
        0% on contract
        <span class="ramp" aria-hidden="true">{% for c in legend %}<span style="background: {{ c }}"></span>{% endfor %}</span>
        100% on contract
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="two">
    <div>
      <h2>What to look at first</h2>
      <p class="lede">The six largest contract and concentration problems, ranked by the spend they concern.</p>
      <ul class="findings">
        {% for c in findings %}
        <li>
          <span class="swatch" style="background: {{ c.on_contract_share|colour }}"></span>
          <span class="cat">{{ c.category }}</span>
          <span class="amt">{{ c.at_stake|eur_short }}</span>
          <span class="msg">{{ c.finding }}</span>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Supplier concentration</h2>
      <p class="lede">Suppliers ranked by spend, largest first. {{ t.tail_suppliers }} suppliers together make up the last 5%: purchase cards or a catalogue would cost less to run than purchase orders.</p>
      <figure class="pareto">{{ pareto|safe }}</figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if groups %}
  <section>
    <h2>Supplier groups</h2>
    <p class="lede">Subsidiaries and joint ventures rolled up to their parent group. Joint-venture spend is split between the owners by their share.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th class="n">Spend</th><th class="n">Companies</th><th class="n">Countries</th><th class="n">On contract</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for g in groups %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ g.group }}<span class="sub">{{ g.member_names|join("; ") }}{% if g.has_joint_venture %} (includes a joint venture share){% endif %}</span></td>
            <td class="n">{{ g.spend|eur }}</td>
            <td class="n">{{ g.members }}</td>
            <td class="n">{{ g.countries }}</td>
            <td class="n">{{ g.on_contract_share|pct }}<span class="cov" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width: {{ (g.on_contract_share * 100)|round(1) }}%"></span></span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if suggestions %}
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 16px"><strong>Possibly related, not in the group map:</strong>
      {% for s in suggestions %}{{ s.suppliers }} ({{ s.spend|eur_short }}){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Check and add them to the map if they belong together.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>Categories</h2>
    <p class="lede">HHI measures concentration from 0 to 10,000; above 2,500 a few suppliers dominate, below 1,500 spend is spread thin. Group HHI counts companies of the same group as one.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Category</th><th class="n">Spend</th><th class="n">Suppliers</th><th>Largest supplier</th><th class="n">HHI</th><th class="n">Group HHI</th><th class="n">On contract</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in categories %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ c.category }}<span class="sub">{{ c.category_group }}</span></td>
            <td class="n">{{ c.spend|eur }}</td>
            <td class="n">{{ c.suppliers }}</td>
            <td>{{ c.top_supplier }}<span class="sub">{{ c.top_share|pct }} of category</span></td>
            <td class="n">{{ "{:,.0f}".format(c.hhi) }}</td>
            <td class="n{% if c.group_hhi > c.hhi + 500 %} up{% endif %}">{{ "{:,.0f}".format(c.group_hhi) }}</td>
            <td class="n">{{ c.on_contract_share|pct }}<span class="cov" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width: {{ (c.on_contract_share * 100)|round(1) }}%"></span></span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if yoy %}
  <section>
    <h2>Year on year</h2>
    <p class="lede">Spend from {{ yoy_period.current[0]|day }} to {{ yoy_period.current[1]|day }} against the same days a year earlier, largest changes first. Comparing the same days keeps seasonal swings out of it. {% if t.yoy_rising_off_contract %}<strong>{{ t.yoy_rising_off_contract }} {{ "category is" if t.yoy_rising_off_contract == 1 else "categories are" }} growing fast with most spend off contract</strong>, which is where a sourcing event pays first.{% endif %}</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Category</th><th class="n">This year</th><th class="n">Same days last year</th><th class="n">Change</th><th class="n">On contract</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for y in yoy %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ y.category }}<span class="sub">{{ y.category_group }}{% if y.rising_off_contract %} · growing off contract{% endif %}</span></td>
            <td class="n">{{ y.current|eur }}</td>
            <td class="n">{{ y.prior|eur }}</td>
            <td class="n{% if y.rising_off_contract %} up{% endif %}">{{ y.change_eur|signed_eur }}<span class="sub">{{ y.change|signed_pct }}</span></td>
            <td class="n">{{ y.on_contract_share|pct }}<span class="cov" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width: {{ (y.on_contract_share * 100)|round(1) }}%"></span></span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="two">
    <div>
      <h2>One supplier, many names</h2>
      <p class="lede">The largest suppliers and the spellings that were merged into them.</p>
      {% for m in merges %}
      <div class="merge">
        <div class="to">{{ m.supplier }} <span class="sub" style="color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400">{{ m.spend|eur_short }}</span></div>
        <div class="from">{{ m.spellings|join("; ") }}</div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>How each line was classified</h2>
      <p class="lede">Share of spend by the layer that assigned its category.</p>
      <div class="stack" role="img" aria-label="Classification sources">
        {% for s in sources %}<span style="width: {{ (s.share * 100)|round(2) }}%; background: {{ s.colour }}" title="{{ s.label }}: {{ s.share|pct }}"></span>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="stack-legend">
        {% for s in sources %}<span><i style="background: {{ s.colour }}"></i>{{ s.label }} {{ s.share|pct }}</span>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <h2 style="margin-top: 32px">Review queue</h2>
      <p class="lede">{{ review_count }} lines worth {{ review_value|eur_short }} have no category or a low-confidence one. The largest:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Supplier</th><th>Description</th><th class="n">Amount</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for r in review %}
            <tr><td>{{ r.supplier }}</td><td>{{ r.description }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.amount_eur|eur }}</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Method</h2>
    <div class="method">
      <p><strong>Suppliers.</strong> Names are folded (umlauts, case, punctuation), legal forms and locations removed, then matched within each country by fuzzy similarity and joined with union-find. A guard stops merges when the words that differ are unrelated, so "Becker Elektro" and "Becker Druck" stay apart.</p>
      <p><strong>Categories.</strong> Keyword rules in English and German come first. Lines a rule cannot place inherit the category of their supplier when at least 80% of that supplier's classified spend sits in one category. An optional language model handles what remains, seeing only line descriptions, never supplier names or amounts.</p>
      <p><strong>Groups.</strong> A group map assigns suppliers to their parent group, with an ownership share for joint ventures. Suppliers not in the map are their own group. Suppliers in different countries whose names start with the same distinctive word, but share no group, are listed for review.</p>
      <p><strong>Contracts.</strong> A line counts as on contract when its purchase order references a contract. Spend outside contracts in a category that has a contract is reported as leakage.</p>
      <p><strong>Concentration.</strong> HHI is the sum of squared supplier shares within a category, on a 0 to 10,000 scale. The long tail is the set of smallest suppliers that together account for 5% of spend.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    Generated {{ generated }} by <a href="https://github.com/awaisq5/procurement-spend-cube">procurement-spend-cube</a>. Sample data is synthetic; supplier names are invented. Independent personal project: it contains no information from any former employer. The extracts behind this report are in classified_lines.csv, supplier_map.csv and review_queue.csv.
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
